<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Saxony</h1><p class="st-meta">1806 CE – 1918 CE · capital Dresden</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kingdom of the Albertine Wettins created under Napoleon, a German industrial heartland around Dresden, Leipzig and Chemnitz.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-augustus-iii-of-saxony">Frederick Augustus III of Saxony</a> changed sides after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia's</a> defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a> and joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a> in December 1806, taking the title King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-augustus-i-of-saxony">Frederick Augustus I</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> also made him Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> in 1807.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> fought for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a> in 1813, and at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> it lost about three-fifths of its territory to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>. A constitution followed the unrest of 1830, and the May Uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a> in 1849 was crushed with Prussian help. Textiles, machine building and mining made Saxony one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany's</a> most industrialised regions, and Leipzig was a centre of publishing and music.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1866, then joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-german-confederation">North German Confederation</a> and in 1871 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-augustus-iii-of-saxony">King Frederick Augustus III</a> abdicated in November 1918, and the state became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-state-of-saxony">Free State of Saxony</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-saxony.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Saxony" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Rössel (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:State_flag_of_Saxony_before_1815.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1806 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dresden</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Frederick Augustus I, John, Frederick Augustus III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a>, <a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Königreich Sachsen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1862&amp;focus=kingdom-of-saxony" aria-label="Kingdom of Saxony on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4992 408 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Saxony lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5312 664L5325 660M5312 664L5312 664M5312 664L5199 691M5312 664L5473 630M5312 664L5199 691M5312 664L5300 622M5312 664L5300 622M5312 664L5312 664"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5325 660h0M5312 664h0M5199 691h0M5473 630h0M5199 691h0M5300 622h0M5300 622h0M5312 664h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5312 664h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5312 664h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dresden. <a href="/atlas?year=1862&amp;focus=kingdom-of-saxony">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
